      "writtenOn": "2023-06-06T15:40:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Their variable naming uses a more restrictive definition of \"MMIO\", I guess? The UART (see `AARCH64_SERIAL_SIZE`) at page `0x0`, RTC (`AARCH64_RTC_ADDR`) or watchdog (`AARCH64_VMWDT_ADDR`) would all count as (virtual) MMIO devices. For the range above (`0x400_0000` to `0x4000_0000`), it\u0027s less clear but it is fair to assume that we shouldn\u0027t have more normal memory there (they already have the memory-mapped vGIC) and, as crosvm devs have modified their platform layout to accommodate new devices in the past, I\u0027d rather have a flexible implementation which we don\u0027t need to tweak unnecessarily, TBH.",
      "parentUuid": "d2d95320_e00c6632",
